+  "task_id": "session-migration/learn",
+  "repository": "earendil-works/pi",
+  "mode": "repair",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "claim": "Legacy oauth.json with a UTF-8 BOM no longer migrates.",
+      "evidence": "packages/coding-agent/src/migrations.ts:36 parsed oauth.json with a bare JSON.parse(readFileSync(...)) while settings.json/keybindings.json already used stripBom(); JSON.parse rejects a leading U+FEFF, so the throw was swallowed and nothing migrated."
+    },
+    {
+      "claim": "OAuth credentials, API-key fallback and OAuth precedence are preserved.",
+      "evidence": "Regression cases 'oauth.json with a UTF-8 BOM migrates its OAuth credentials', 'settings.json apiKeys still migrate when no oauth.json exists' and 'OAuth credentials take precedence over colliding apiKeys' assert the resulting auth.json payloads, not just return codes."
+    },
+    {
+      "claim": "Malformed input must not be destroyed.",
+      "evidence": "Regression cases 'malformed oauth.json is never destroyed', 'malformed oauth.json keeps the API-key fallback available' and 'malformed settings.json is never rewritten' assert byte-identical files and absence of oauth.json.migrated."
+    },
+    {
+      "claim": "Existing auth.json must remain untouched.",
+      "evidence": "Regression case 'an existing auth.json is left untouched and short-circuits migration' asserts byte-identical auth.json, untouched oauth.json/settings.json and an empty provider list."
+    }
+  ],
+  "deliverables": [
+    "packages/coding-agent/src/migrations.ts",
+    ".prale-eval/regression.mjs"
+  ],
+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "Fix is one line in migrateAuthToAuthJson: JSON.parse(stripBom(readFileSync(oauthPath, \"utf-8\"))), matching the stripBom already used for settings.json, keybindings.json and auth-storage.ts; no other behavior, control flow or file handling changed. The regression is a standalone Node 24 assertion script (node:assert/strict, no dependencies, no network) that loads the real migrations.ts through the read-only .prale-eval/subject.mjs helper with only getAgentDir/stripBom faked and real fs/path, using throwaway agent dirs under .prale-eval/tmp-* that are removed in a finally block. It runs 10 assertion cases: plain oauth.json baseline; BOM oauth.json migration including provider list, credential payload, 0o600 auth.json mode, oauth.json.migrated rename and preserved original bytes; BOM oauth + settings apiKeys side by side; API-key fallback with BOM settings; OAuth precedence over a colliding api key; malformed oauth.json preserved verbatim with no .migrated rename and no auth.json; malformed oauth.json plus working api-key fallback; malformed settings.json preserved verbatim; existing auth.json byte-identical short-circuit; idempotent re-run. Verified locally: exit 0 with 'ok - 10 migration regression cases passed' against the repaired source, and exit 1 with AssertionError 'BOM oauth.json must report migrated providers' (actual [] vs expected ['anthropic','openai-codex']) on an isolated copy of migrations.ts with stripBom removed for oauth.json, i.e. it fails as a real assertion, not a syntax/import/runtime error. Cross-realm VM arrays are normalized with a JSON round-trip before deepEqual because the module evaluates in its own context. Optional validations (biome format check and tsgo typecheck) were not run because node_modules is not installed in this workspace and dependencies must not be installed; the one-line change keeps the existing tab style and stays within the 120-column formatter width."
+  }
+}
